// The entry module: `use App.Models.User` resolves to the real `User` class declared in the
// sibling `Models.noe` (not an opaque stub), so its constructor, fields, and methods are real.
// The linker merges the resolved declaration into one program, so both backends run it
// identically (the differential oracle).
// expect: stdout "Ada"
// expect: stdout "7"
// expect: stdout "Hi, Ada"
// expect: exit 0

use App.Models.User;

customer = User.new("Ada", 7);
echo customer.name;
echo customer.id;
echo customer.greeting();
